  "pitch_paragraph": "Built on contrast — it runs at full energy for the first thirty-four seconds, cuts out hard, and lets the chorus hit from the drop, a move it repeats before all three. The topline is demanding: it lives around A4 through the body and reaches A5, so it wants a singer with genuine top end rather than one who'll ask to take it down a step. The chorus doesn't land until 0:48, which reads as a deliberate build and is also the obvious thing to tighten for a single edit. Warmer and wider than most current K-pop masters, with real room in the stereo field for stacks and ad-libs.",
